    "recommendations": "• Mark each access point with visible address signage so responders can quickly identify the correct entry from the street.\n\n• Mark the rear access route with directional signage indicating which building or loading area it serves.\n\n• Keep the loading area clear of stored materials to allow emergency vehicles to stage or approach the building.\n\n• Mark the secondary building with its own visible identifier so responders can distinguish it from the main building during an incident.\n\n• Keep the internal drive aisle clear of parked vehicles and equipment to allow unobstructed movement between structures.\n\n• Mark the dumpster enclosure location on any posted site map so responders can avoid confusing it with other structures in low-visibility conditions.\n\n• Post a site map at each access point showing building locations, the internal drive aisle, the loading area, and the limited rear access route.\n\n• Keep outdoor storage consolidated and away from building walls to allow responders to move around the structures without obstruction."
